# netsurf: -webkit-line-clamp / line-clamp clamp the box to N lines (patch 208, needs 207's lh)
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser f352150 (patch stack through 205)
#
# Card titles and summaries on news, shop and blog pages clamp to N lines
# with display: -webkit-box; -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
# -webkit-line-clamp: N; overflow: hidden. modern_compat dropped the
# clamp, so every clamped block showed all of its text and the cards grew
# to fit. macsurf__rewrite_line_clamp (run just before modern_compat, on
# stylesheets and style="" alike) rewrites an integer -webkit-line-clamp
# or line-clamp to `max-height: Nlh`: the legacy WebKit clamp sizes the
# box to N lines and lets the rest overflow, which is what that does; the
# page's own overflow: hidden cuts the text. No ellipsis is drawn, and
# the clamp applies whether or not display: -webkit-box is in effect
# (pages set them together). Non-integer values are still dropped.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/CSS-line-clamp.html (CLAMP208, 4 checks,
# Chromium 4/4; 1/4 without 206-208): clamp 2 at 20px lines is 40px, an
# inline-style clamp 3 is 60px, a one-line text keeps its line, a
# line-height: normal clamp lands within Chromium's font-dependent range.
diff --git a/content/handlers/css/css_rewrite.c b/content/handlers/css/css_rewrite.c
--- a/content/handlers/css/css_rewrite.c
+++ b/content/handlers/css/css_rewrite.c
@@ -3564,6 +3564,114 @@
